    "## Phase 1 \u2014 Deep latent compression\n",
    "\n",
    "### 1.1 Architecture design (10 pts)\n",
    "\n",
    "Encoder: five stride-2 convolutional stages, 224 -> 112 -> 56 -> 28 -> 14 -> 7, channel widths\n",
    "32, 64, 128, 256, 256, each stage a strided conv followed by a 3x3 conv, GroupNorm and SiLU.\n",
    "The 256x7x7 map is flattened and projected by a single linear layer to a fixed-length latent\n",
    "vector, so every image produces the same 1D vector required by Phase 2.\n",
    "\n",
    "Decoder: mirror of the encoder, but upsampling is nearest-neighbour resize followed by a 3x3\n",
    "conv instead of a transposed conv. Transposed convs with stride 2 and even kernels put a\n",
    "periodic checkerboard into the reconstruction, which then shows up as a false grid pattern in\n",
    "the Phase 3 error heatmaps.\n",
    "\n",
    "Latent dimensionality: 256. At 128 the reconstructions lose dune crest detail, and at 512 the\n",
    "Isolation Forest degrades, because each tree splits on one randomly chosen coordinate at a\n",
    "time, so adding coordinates that carry little variance dilutes the probability of ever\n",
    "splitting on an informative one. 256 keeps reconstruction sharp while still allowing a PCA\n",
    "step in Phase 2 to concentrate the variance into a few dozen coordinates for the forest.\n",
    "A VAE variant is included behind `CFG[\"model\"] = \"vae\"`; the deterministic autoencoder is the\n",
    "default because a KL term pulls all latents toward the prior, which shrinks the very\n",
    "separation the forest needs.\n",
    "\n",
    "No pretrained weights, no external feature extractor, no transfer learning is used anywhere."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
