    "### 2.3 Image location analysis (6 pts)\n",
    "\n",
    "The crop-level scores are joined to the provided source metadata by `source_image_id`. Three\n",
    "questions are asked of the join: whether novelty varies with sun angle (Spearman, since the\n",
    "relation need not be linear), whether it varies by season (Kruskal-Wallis, since the score\n",
    "distribution is skewed), and whether any individual source observation contributes more flagged\n",
    "crops than the archive-wide rate would predict (one-sided binomial test per source, corrected\n",
    "across the roughly 180 sources with Benjamini-Hochberg).\n",
    "\n",
    "The per-source test is the one that matters for the geology. If flags were scattered uniformly\n",
    "across sources they would look like isolated frames; if they concentrate in a handful of\n",
    "observations, then either those observations contain unusual terrain or they were the frames\n",
    "that were tampered with."
   ]
