    "\n",
    "Error concentrated along a linear feature, high coherence: a straight discontinuity that the\n",
    "encoder cannot represent. On Mars a natural candidate is a scarp, a graben wall, or a fresh\n",
    "ridge crest; an artificial candidate is a splice seam where two crops were joined, which is\n",
    "distinguishable because a splice seam usually runs to both frame edges and has no shadow\n",
    "consistent with the sun angle in the metadata.\n",
    "\n",
    "Error concentrated in a compact blob: a local structure with no counterpart in the training\n",
    "distribution. Fresh impact craters with rayed ejecta and recurring slope lineae both produce\n",
    "this, as does an object pasted into the frame. The sun-angle column decides between them: a\n",
    "real feature casts a shadow on the anti-solar side, a pasted object usually does not.\n",
    "\n",
    "Error hugging the frame edge: a crop boundary artefact or a partial-overlap splice, since\n",
    "genuine terrain has no reason to become harder to reconstruct only at the border.\n",
    "\n",
    "Error fine-grained and spread over the frame, low Moran's I: detector-level noise, a compression\n",
    "or bit-error artefact, or a dropped-line sensor fault. The autoencoder reproduces terrain\n",
    "statistics but cannot reproduce noise that has no spatial structure.\n",
